ory. Never expose secrets or credential values. DOCKER/CONTAINER RULE: if Docker/devcontainer validation is required by repository policy, CI parity or mission acceptance and no compatible daemon is available, classify that gate BLOCKED_EXTERNAL, not NOT_RUN and not PASS; if it is genuinely optional for the current scope, classify NOT_APPLICABLE with exact justification. REMOTE CI: when gh/API access is available, inspect actual runs for ORIGIN and CANONICAL_UPSTREAM. For every cited run record repository, workflow name, run ID, run URL, event, branch, HEAD_SHA, status and conclusion. A successful run validates a target only when its HEAD_SHA equals the exact commit being claimed or when ancestry plus workflow semantics explicitly justify the claim. Never use an older successful origin run to validate LOCAL_HEAD. If no runs are returned, report only NO_VISIBLE_RUNS or NOT_VERIFIABLE_REMOTE; do not speculate that CI is private, disabled or absent without direct evidence. STATUS SEMANTICS: GREEN_UPSTREAM_VALIDATED = applicable local gates pass, validated implementation is confirmed at canonical upstream, and all applicable required remote gates for that exact upstream commit are verified; GREEN_FORK_VALIDATED = applicable local gates pass and implementation is confirmed at origin, but not canonical upstream, with applicable origin remote gates correlated to the exact origin commit; GREEN_LOCAL_VALIDATED = all applicable achievable local gates pass, implementation remains LOCAL_ONLY or LOCAL_AHEAD_ORIGIN, and no applicable gate is BLOCKED_EXTERNAL or NOT_RUN; YELLOW_EXTERNAL_BLOCKER = at least one applicable gate is BLOCKED_EXTERNAL; RED_UNRESOLVED = applicable gate failed or material defect remains unresolved. NOT_APPLICABLE never counts as executed. NOT_RUN never equals PASS. If any applicable gate is NOT_RUN, final state cannot be GREEN*. If any applicable gate is BLOCKED_EXTERNAL, final state must be YELLOW_EXTERNAL_BLOCKER even if all executed gates passed. EVIDENCE DISCIPLINE: never claim 0 regressions unless the full applicable regression surface was executed. Never claim 100% validation when Docker/build/E2E/remote CI required by scope is blocked or unexecuted. Never claim zero unintended writes, 100% preservation, clean diff, deployment readiness, full alignment or all invariants verified without direct before/after proof. Distinguish 'all executed gates passed' from 'all applicable gates executed'. Every material conclusion must cite command, exit code, SHA, merge-base, ahead/behind count, diff, status, hash, mutation count, test output, remote-run evidence or policy reference. FINISH with an Evidence Ledger containing TARGET; BRANCH; LOCAL_HEAD; ORIGIN_URL/HEAD; UPSTREAM_URL/HEAD; LOCAL_vs_ORIGIN metrics; ORIGIN_vs_UPSTREAM metrics; LOCAL_vs_UPSTREAM metrics; policies; complete GATE_INVENTORY; architecture; UPSTREAM_CONFIRMED; ORIGIN_CONFIRMED; LOCAL_AHEAD_ORIGIN; FORK_ONLY; LOCAL_ONLY; NOT_VERIFIABLE_REMOTE; PRE_EXISTING_MODIFIED; PRE_EXISTING_UNTRACKED; AUTOPILOT_CREATED; AUTOPILOT_MODIFIED; PRE_EXISTING_PRESERVED with proof basis; WORKTREE_MUTATIONS; GIT_METADATA_MUTATIONS; WRITE_SET; BLAST_RADIUS; commands and exit codes; tests; EXECUTED gates; APPLICABLE gates; NOT_APPLICABLE gates with exact justification; BLOCKED_EXTERNAL gates with blocker/evidence/next action; NOT_RUN gates with reason; REMOTE_CI entries with exact HEAD_SHA correlation; failures; root causes; residual risks; precise VALIDATION_SCOPE; and exactly one final state: GREEN_UPSTREAM_VALIDATED, GREEN_FORK_VALIDATED — NOT YET UPSTREAM, GREEN_LOCAL_VALIDATED — NOT YET ON ORIGIN, YELLOW — EXTERNAL BLOCKER, or RED — UNRESOL
